       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's twice the maximum labeled daily dose, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1700 mg/day in divided doses.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** For example, 500 mg or 1000 mg PO twice daily.\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
